{
 "id": "urdf-forearm",
 "brief": "desk_arm.urdf (attached) is my 3-joint desk arm. Design the `forearm` link, SLS PA12, in the\nforearm's own frame in millimetres (the URDF is in metres). At the elbow end (forearm frame\norigin) it bolts to the elbow servo's horn: a 24 mm diameter, 4 mm thick disc in the XZ plane at\ny = 0 to 4 with an 8 mm centre hole along Y and four M2.5 screws on a 16 mm circle (at\n(+/-8, 0) and (0, +/-8) in X-Z). At the wrist end (x = 120 mm) it carries the wrist servo\nthrough a 10 mm wrist bearing along Y at (120, 0, 0) with a 4 mm wall, 8 mm long (y = 0 to 8).\nThe forearm fits in x = -14 to 134, y = 0 to 16, z = -14 to 14. The arm carries 0.4 kg at the\ntool, about 60 mm past the wrist, and moves as fast as its servos allow. Safety factor 2.",
